      "name": "IONodes",
      "objects": [
        {
          "height": 56,
          "id": 3,
          "name": "IOCustomNode",
          "point": false,
          "rotation": 0,
          "type": "IOCustomNode",
          "visible": true,
          "width": 64,
          "x": 921,
          "y": 744,
          "properties": [
            {
              "name": "defaultCode",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "/*\n* \"input\" and \"output\" are variables that are automatically supplied to this\n* node, but the code below shows how we can make a variable of our own\n* called \"crystalTorchValue\" using the \"var\" keyword.\n*\n* Uncomment the lines below to complete the wiring.\n*/\n\n// var crystalTorchValue = input;\n// output = crystalTorchValue;"
            },
            {
              "name": "promptString",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "This node stands in the way of the Crystal Torch and the Tech Door.\n\nThe \"true\" or \"false\" signal from the Crystal Torch is inputted into this node, and is accessible in our code by the special name \"input.\"\n\nThis special name is similar to what we have previously written as \"output.\" These names are both called VARIABLES, which can be thought of as containers that hold values, such as numbers or booleans. In this case, the variable named \"input\" contains the value of either \"true\" or \"false\" from the state of the Crystal Torch.\n\nAnalyze the code below to complete the wiring."
            },
            {
              "name": "titleString",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Complete The Wiring"
            }
          ]
        },
